					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "MULTIPLY & DIVIDE\n\nYou know we couldn't leave it at just addition and subtraction right?\nThe Multiply and Divide node are here to do multiplication and division with your data types.\n\nMultiply can be useful if you want to scale some parameter by a given factor.\nDivide can be useful when working with the resolution of your patch to get things at ½ , ¼ or ⅛ of the resolution.\n\nIn this example we've made a percentage based scale parameter which is a renamed Int In node.\nIt runs from 0 to 100, but the Transform node works in a factor, so 100 would be 100 times the original size. So we divide by 100 to get back into a 0 to 1 range. The end user sees 0 to 100, we do our transformation with 0 to 1.\n"
					}
				},
